{"author":{"id":"8022379585b4ab99ca8775db3eb67d33fcb256817114c28e51ccc1e9f55cdec4"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1791631331,"nonce":"OY9hrKCNKmzBmEAPORZczVIdGfM=","title":"A Class\u003cT\u003e-typed value is boxed as an Int, so Reflect.field on it misses statics","message":"Found triaging conformance row Issue3725 (which also needs @:rtti generation).\n`Reflect.field(c, \"x\")` with `c:Class\u003cT\u003e` returns null even for ordinary statics,\nwhile `var d:Dynamic = C; Reflect.field(d, \"x\")` works. MIR boxes the Class\u003cT\u003e value\nwith haxe_box_int_ptr instead of haxe_box_reference_ptr(token, token), and\nclass_token_of (runtime/src/reflect.rs) rejects an Int box, so the static accessor\nregistry is never consulted. Fix in maybe_box_value_inner (mir helpers/boxing.rs) for\nthe @:coreType Class abstract (null-safe), or accept an Int box whose payload is a\nregistered class id in the runtime.\n\nIssue3725 itself also needs: @:rtti genxml output as a static __rtti string (typed\nfield types, arg names/optional flags); source spelling of literals for value/expr\nattributes (ExprKind::Int loses `0xFFFFFF`); and haxe.rtti.XmlParser fails with\nE0801 ambiguous dynamic `iterator` on an unresolved receiver.","files":null}]}